# CORRECTED DIAGNOSIS (2026-07-30): originally filed as "run_file_jit never
# strips inactive @cfg(<arch>) GLOBAL variants." That premise was checked
# while attempting the fix and found FALSE: run_file_jit's shared
# load_module_with_imports path already calls strip_inactive_cfg_arch_globals
# correctly (module_loader.rs:1655), confirmed by hand-stripping this exact
# source (removing both @cfg lines, leaving one `val PLATFORM_ID = 64`) and
# reproducing the IDENTICAL wrong value with no @cfg present at all. The
# real cause is the more general defect in
# module_global_direct_read_untagged.spl (a plain module-level val/var's
# value is never tag-boxed before flowing into print()/formatting under
# JIT) -- this fixture is a special case of that one, not a distinct @cfg
# bug. Kept as its own fixture because it is still a real, standing
# divergence worth tracking, and because a future fix to the tag-boxing
# defect should make THIS fixture pass too, at which point it is safe to
# drop (or convert to a real @cfg-specific regression test once the
# tag-boxing defect no longer masks it). See
# doc/08_tracking/bug/jit_run_file_pipeline_gaps_2026-07-30.md section 7,
# and section 9 for the full unification with gaps 8 and 9 (same defect,
# different raw values / consumption shapes).
#
# FIXED 2026-07-30 (section 11): the tag-boxing defect predicted above did
# get fixed, and this fixture DOES now pass -- exactly the "convert to a
# real @cfg-specific regression test" outcome anticipated. It now verifies
# the @cfg stripping was never broken (both variants correctly resolve to
# the host literal) with the masking defect gone. known_good is now "both".
# Expected (both engines, correct, host is x86_64): PLATFORM_ID=64
@cfg(x86_64)
val PLATFORM_ID = 64

@cfg(riscv64)
val PLATFORM_ID = 32

fn main():
    print("PLATFORM_ID={PLATFORM_ID}")
